# FULLTRANSCRIPT-RESPONSE-HEADER: where fx v0.0.16 heads an answer in its
# full transcript. Its store makes a completed code block, table or rule an
# entry of its own and opens a new assistant entry on the first text after
# one (appendAssistantCodeBlockOwned, store.zig:3000-3040; the stream's tail,
# :3103-3150@481104fd), and its screen heads an assistant entry alone with
# `<time> · Response` (metadataKind, full_transcript_screen.zig:6028-6056).
# A long first answer makes the record taller than the screen, so each tail
# page shows the newest turns only. Then one turn per case, each shown
# inline and in Ctrl-O: text, a table, text; text, a rule, text; an answer
# that is only a code block; one that ends in a code block; one that opens
# with a code block; two code blocks with only a blank line between them.
# `launch` holds the banner, the binary's revision.
gateway fulltranscript-response-split-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
env TZ=UTC
wait 4
snap launch
type the long one
wait 1
key Enter
wait 6
snap long
type the table
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap table
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-table
key C-o
wait 1
type the rule
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap rule
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-rule
key C-o
wait 1
type only a block
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap block-only
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-block-only
key C-o
wait 1
type ends in a block
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap block-last
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-block-last
key C-o
wait 1
type opens with a block
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap block-first
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-block-first
key C-o
wait 1
type two blocks
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap blocks
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-blocks
key C-o
wait 1
gwlog
